 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance to authorize building material restrictions and requirements for BL2026-1638, a proposed Specific Plan Zoning for properties located at 3139, 3145, 3163, 3165 Brandau Road, Brandau Road (unnumbered) and a portion of 3087 Brandau Road, approximately 1,528 feet northeast of Hoggett Ford Road (47.08 acres), to permit a mixed use development, all of which is described herein (Proposal No. 2026SP-016-001). THE PROPOSED ORDINANCE REQUIRES CERTAIN MATERIALS TO BE RESTRICTED IN THE CONSTRUCTION OF BUILDINGS.\n\n..body\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\n\nSection 1. That the following building material restrictions and requirements as a part of BL2026-1638, a proposed Specific Plan Zoning District located located at 3139, 3145, 3163, 3165 Brandau Road, Brandau Road (unnumbered) and a portion of 3087 Brandau Road, approximately 1,528 feet northeast of Hoggett Ford Road (47.08 acres), are hereby authorized:\n\nBuilding facades shall be constructed of wood, log, brick, brick veneer, stone, cast stone, cementitious siding, and glass, or materials substantially similar in form and function, unless otherwise approved on detailed building elevations included with the preliminary SP.\n\nSection 2. That this ordinance take effect immediately after its passage and such change be published in a newspaper of general circulation, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n\n"
